OpenLiteSpeed 1.9.3 — macOS portability (source files only).

Origin: puleeno/homebrew-openlitespeed patches/ols191-macos.patch (GPL-3.0,
written for 1.9.1), cut down by rexenv/runtimes on 4 Oct 2026 to the C/C++ hunks
that still apply to 1.9.3. Dropped, and why:
  - every Makefile.am / configure.ac / ax_path_lib_pcre.m4 / dist/ hunk — we
    build with CMake (upstream's own build.sh path), not autotools;
  - src/http/useacme.cpp and src/extensions/cgi/lscgid.cpp — upstream 1.9.3
    already carries its own fix for both (the VLA initialiser; non-Linux stubs
    for the namespace code), and the tap's hunks fight it.
What remains guards Linux-only calls (posix_fallocate, futex, IP_PKTINFO
shape, <bits/types.h>, kinfo_proc field names) behind #ifdef so the same
source builds on Darwin. Every hunk is inert on Linux.

